Package: MOREcells
Title: Regulatory network inference in single-cell multiomic scenarios
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    c(person(given ="Roxana Andreea", family ="Moldovan", email = "roxana.andreea.moldovan@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6822-0224")),
    person(given ="Ana", family ="Conesa", role = "aut"),
    person(given ="Sonia", family ="Tarazona", role = "aut"))
Description: MOREcells is an R framework designed to analyze gene regulation and multi-omic single-cell data by modeling target omic expression as a function of experimental variables (such as biological conditions, treatments, and cell types) alongside potential regulators of a given target feature, while fully maintaining single-cell resolution and hierarchical data structure. To achieve this, MOREcells utilizes a two-step approach that combines Generalized Linear Mixed Models (GLMMs) to account for donor-specific random effects and prevent pseudoreplication, with flexible post-hoc inference options that allow researchers to infer phenotype-specific regulatory networks and perform custom statistical contrasts across different biological groups.
